  "notes": [
    "MODEL INPUTS: Only the paper-cup PE layer (15 g/m2, ~16 um at 0.92 g/cm3; up to ~40% thinner for ultrathin grades) and the PET coating on ovenable board (40 g/m2, 29 um) have layer data. No measured additive content c_P0 inside the PE or PET layer itself was found; all content data are whole-item (paper+coating) or per area. Park 2016 phthalates (whole cup mg/kg) cannot be assigned to the PE layer because phthalates in paper cups may sit in ink or recycled fibre.",
    "RECOMMENDED APPROACH for paper containers: measurement-based estimates rather than diffusion modelling. Paper is porous and PFAS/MOH transfer via gas phase and fat wicking, which Piringer-type PE/PET models do not represent.",
    "Best microwave dataset: Lerch et al. 2022 (1 min, 800 W, PFAS-treated paper plates). Illustrative worst case (assumptions: 300 g serving, 70 kg adult): tomato soup plate C 0.63 ng PFOA-eq/g x 300 g = 189 ng = 2.7 ng/kg bw = ~61% of the 4.4 ng/kg bw/week TWI per serving; on the strict PFAS4 basis (PFOA+PFNA 0.05 ng/g) = 15 ng = 0.21 ng/kg bw = ~5% TWI. These items were legacy PFAS-treated (Scandinavia 2017-2019); US products after the Feb 2024 FDA announcement should not carry intentionally added PFAS grease-proofing.",
    "Paper cup hot water (Mohery 2025): Pb median 1.38 ug/L -> ~0.28 ug per 200 mL cup; Ranjan 2021: ~25,000 microplastic particles per 100 mL at 85-90 C/15 min (no tox reference value; report count only).",
    "Susceptors reach >200 C within 1-2 min (Begley 2005). Historic BADGE migration 0.1-0.7 mg/kg into pizza (1992 UK) shows susceptor adhesives can migrate; no post-2010 susceptor migration data found.",
    "No antimony data for PET-coated paperboard were found. Existing CPET Sb data (Haldimann 2007/2013, already in substances.json) are the closest proxy; PET coating mass is ~40 g/m2.",
    "No measured MOSH/MOAH, photoinitiator, PFAS or primary aromatic amine migration specifically from instant-noodle paper cups or paper bowls under microwave heating was found. Pack 2020 (Korea) is the closest MOSH/MOAH dataset (25 C/10 min, ug/L in fatty simulant).",
    "Unit cautions: Begley 2005 values were reconciled by arithmetic (PFOA in bag 6-290 ug/kg; PFOA migration <1 ug/kg oil; telomer additive 2.1 mg/kg oil ~7 ug/dm2). Fraunhofer 2012 muffin migration (3594 ng/dm2) exceeds the listed cp0 (636 ng/dm2) in the source table; treat as reported, not re-derived.",
    "Access problems this session: PubMed and PMC pages returned captcha/redirect; Europe PMC REST returned HTTP 429 (rate limited) and the Norwegian Mattilsynet PFAS-in-paper report URL was too long to fetch; BfR PFAS migration PDF fetch failed. WebSearch quota was exhausted before searching recycled-board phthalate migration data and post-2023 US popcorn-bag PFAS measurements, so those remain open.",
    "Not found / open items: PE lining thickness measured in Ranjan 2021; ion and metal concentrations from Ranjan 2021; ITX/benzophenone migration from printed paper cups into hot water (only material detection in Kiralan 2026); primary aromatic amines from paper cups; any US popcorn bag PFAS concentrations measured after the 2024 FDA announcement."
